From 37b064f06f4741c840ccd17354f6e01ff2698125 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lolzen <funer@gmx.at>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:06:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] screenreader: Run the screen reader without systemd --user

The screen reader appeared only after the session manager saw the
gamescope-session user unit become active, and Orca was started as the
orca user unit. Without a user service manager, as on runit systems,
neither exists.

There, steamos-manager runs inside the login session it serves and ends
with it, so the login mode is taken from the session's XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP
and stays fixed while the daemon runs. Orca is started as a child process
the way orca.service starts it, with the variables of
$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/gamescope-environment when that file exists. systemd
systems are unchanged.
